                "text": "<p>A container gets made. It sells to a national distributor, who marks it up. Then to a regional distributor, who marks it up. Then to your local rep, who marks it up again. By the time you pay, the price has very little to do with what the thing cost to make.</p><p>We buy direct from the factory and sell direct to you. Same grade the established brands carry. The savings come out of the supply chain, not out of the product.</p>"
